@startuml 06-state-machine
!include _style.iuml
title Incident lifecycle (enforced by IncidentStateMachine)
hide empty description
skinparam ranksep 40

state NEW
state CLASSIFIED : priority + SLA deadlines set
state ASSIGNED : technician chosen by strategy
state ACKNOWLEDGED : response time met
state IN_PROGRESS
state PENDING_INFO #FFF4DC : SLA clock paused
state RESOLVED : resolution recorded
state VERIFIED : reporter confirms
state CLOSED #E5F4E5
state CANCELLED #ECEBE7
state DUPLICATE #ECEBE7

[*] --> NEW : employee reports
NEW --> CLASSIFIED : priority calculated
CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : auto / admin assigns
ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : technician
ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : start work
IN_PROGRESS --> PENDING_INFO : request info
PENDING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : reporter answers
IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolve
RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : reporter verifies
RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : reopen
VERIFIED --> CLOSED : feedback / admin close
CLOSED --> [*]

NEW --> CANCELLED
CLASSIFIED --> CANCELLED
ASSIGNED --> CANCELLED : reporter / admin
NEW --> DUPLICATE
CLASSIFIED --> DUPLICATE
ASSIGNED --> DUPLICATE
ACKNOWLEDGED --> DUPLICATE : admin marks
CANCELLED --> [*]
DUPLICATE --> [*]

note right of NEW
  Any other move, e.g. NEW → CLOSED,
  throws InvalidStateTransitionException
  (HTTP 409 through the API).
end note
@enduml
